<nowrap><font color=white>Posted by <A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=918&lastnode_id=1687">Skiks</a> on 2001-04-28 10:18:49</font></nowrap></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan=2>ssSkiks would like to requesst all of the Bloodfist Battalion (lvl 27 -35) to hunt with him in the Miness of Nurga in the Frontier Mountainss. It filled with all sssortss of ugly goblinss. It iss ideal for sseveral reassons. Here they be:<br>
1. Very good place to hone all sskillss. (ooc: 12% exp bonus)<br>
2. There iss a bind sspot only 1 min run away! <br>
3. The treassure iss alsso very nice.<br>
4. Itss about time the Bloodfist Battalion made a solid sshowing of itss ability on its own to the older memberss of the Bloodhorde. <br>
<br>
Thiss iss a great place to hunt. I have sscouted it out sseveral timess now. Once with Zmaka. I am ssure sshe can tell you how good it lookss. I have found sseveral good trickss to pulling ssingless in there to avoid the 4 goblin trainss that are easily possible (the largesst train I was able to create was 6 goblinss). With a good full on assault of one solid group, the first room could be the perfect pulling area. The front room has a sspawn of 4, with a re-sspawn time of 8 mins with each ssingal sspawn having a 1 min time gap between the next sspawn to each of the total 4 (12 min total to full re-sspawn.)<br>
<br>
Pleassse let Skiks know (ooc:in game or here) when you can be there. I will be trying to get all of the Bloodfist Battalion to hunt there all week. I would like to sstart the invasssion tomorrow. You may want to get a map before you go. The besst one I have sseen so far iss at: <br>
http://www.eqatlas.com/kunark.nurga1map.html<br>
<br>
(OOC: I hope I am not being to presumptious with this call to arms, but I felt since we have no Dragoon or Crusader at the time someone should take some initiative and get our Battalion active.)<br>
 <br>
ssSee all you Bloodfistss ssoon!<br>
-Skiks<br>
<br>
PS: I would recommend that if you cannot inviss yoursself, to buy 2 inviss potions (13pp each from alchemy venders {cloudy potionss they are called}) for emergency exitss. I will have sseveral extra on me jusst in casse.<br>
<br>
